{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "Prior Approval",
  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - Any development under Class A is permitted subject to the condition that it must be completed within a period of 3 years starting with the date prior approval is granted.\nReason: To comply with Schedule 2, Part 20, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "Condition : 2 - Any development under Class A is permitted subject to the condition that before beginning the development, the developer must provide the local planning authority with a report for the management of the construction of the development, which sets out the proposed development hours of operation and how any adverse impact of noise, dust, vibration and traffic on occupiers of the building and adjoining owners or occupiers will be mitigated.\nReason: To comply with Schedule 2, Part 20, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "Condition : 3 - The developer must notify the local planning authority of the completion of the development as soon as reasonably practicable after completion. The notification referred to must be in writing and must include:\n(a) the name of the developer;\n(b) the address or location of the development; and \n(c) the date of completion\nReason: To comply with Schedule 2, Part 20, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "Condition : 4 - Any new dwellinghouse created under Class A is to remain in use as a dwellinghouse within the meaning of Class C3 of the Schedule to the Use Classes Order and for no other purpose, except to the extent that the other purpose is ancillary to the primary use as a dwellinghouse.\nReason: To comply with Schedule 2, Part 20, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to occupation of the dwellings hereby approved the communal cycle store with space for 18 bicycles as shown on drawing: 1101 Rev. 1 shall be provided and shall thereafter be kept available for the parking of bicycles\nReason: In order to support sustainable transport objectives.",
    "Condition : 6 - Prior to occupation of the dwellings hereby approved the formally arranged car parking layout shown on drawing 1101 Rev. 1 shall be implemented and maintained thereafter.\nReason: In order to ensure that sufficient parking spaces are made available and in the interests of the safety and efficiency of the local transport network.",
    "Condition : 7 - Before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, a Car Parking Management Plan shall first be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with the approved details and shall be maintained for the lifetime of the development, unless the prior written approval of the local planning authority is obtained to secure any variation. \nReason: In order to control the level and usage of parking on the site and to support sustainable transport objectives."
  ],
